            {
              "type": "Consult Note",
              "title": "Psychiatry Follow-up Letter",
              "author": "psychiatry",
              "date": "2026-02-27T11:10",
              "body": "Community behavioral health clinic, update. Visit 2/24/2026.\n\nTitration went smoothly. Now clozapine 100 mg at bedtime (one 100 mg tablet). No fever on his log, no stiffness. Some morning grogginess and more saliva at night; using a towel on the pillow. Bowels regular. Voices a little quieter; sleeping through the night for the first time in months.\n\nANC normal every week, CK flat at his baseline. Thank you for the draws.\nPlan: hold at 100 mg for 6 weeks, then consider 150 mg.\nAllergies: risperidone (NMS), aripiprazole (NMS)."
            }
