          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Progress Notes",
              "title": "Office Visit",
              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2026-03-10T11:15",
              "body": "Check-in eight weeks into clozapine (psychiatry managing; 100 mg at bedtime since late February).\n\nHe says he feels \"less crowded in my head.\" Sleeping well, a bit slow in the mornings. Drools on the pillow some nights. Bowels every day or two, no straining. No fever, no stiffness, temperature log normal. Eating more; weight up about 1.5 kg. Back at the gym twice a week, easy pace, no cramps.\n\nMeds: clozapine 100 mg qhs (psychiatry). Intolerances: risperidone, aripiprazole (both NMS).\n\nExam: weight 75 kg. BP, HR normal, afebrile. Brighter, better eye contact, organized. No rigidity, no tremor. Heart regular. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, bowel sounds normal, nontender.\n\nPHQ-9 4.\n\nA/P:\n1) Schizophrenia on clozapine: tolerating. Weekly CBC/ANC and CK continue; drawn today with a BMP. Watch weight; A1c and lipids at his physical.\n2) Bowel habits fine for now; he knows to call if he goes 3 days without a movement, a known clozapine problem.\n3) GSD IV: stable, neuromuscular next week.\nReturn in August for the physical."
            }
