          "documents": [
            {
              "type": "Consult Note",
              "title": "Neuromuscular Clinic Annual Follow-up",
              "author": "neurology",
              "date": "2026-03-20T14:00",
              "body": "NEUROMUSCULAR CLINIC\nVisit 3/17/2026. GSD IV, neuromuscular form.\n\nInterval: second NMS in October 2025 on aripiprazole, recovered. Started clozapine in January under psychiatry with weekly CK through primary care, all at his baseline.\n\nExam: full strength throughout, reflexes normal, no organomegaly, no rigidity.\n\nImpression: stable myopathy. No new muscle concerns with clozapine so far.\nRecommendations: continue CK monitoring with the ANC draws; hydrate; moderate exercise only. Echo and liver ultrasound due next year (3 years from 2023). Return in one year.\nAllergies: risperidone (NMS), aripiprazole (NMS). Meds: clozapine 100 mg at bedtime.\nNeuromuscular attending"
            }
          ]
        },
