              "author": "PCP",
              "date": "2026-08-14T10:05",
              "body": "Annual exam, 26 y/o.\n\nProblems: schizophrenia, on clozapine 150 mg qhs since April (psychiatry), good response; GSD IV, neuromuscular form, stable (neuromuscular 3/2026); NMS x2 (risperidone 10/2024, aripiprazole 10/2025), resolved.\nIntolerances: risperidone, aripiprazole (NMS).\n\nInterval: \"the most normal year in a while.\" Volunteering two mornings a week, enrolled for a community college class in January. Voices rare and quiet. Sleeping 9 hours. Still drools at night. Bowels daily. Gym twice a week, easy pace, no cramps or dark urine. No substances, no tobacco, no alcohol. Labs every 2 weeks now, all fine.\n\nExam: weight 77 kg, up about 3.5 kg over the year on clozapine. Vitals normal, afebrile. Well groomed, bright, good eye contact, organized speech. HEENT normal. Heart regular, no murmur. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft, nontender, no hepatosplenomegaly. Strength 5/5, tone normal, no tremor. Skin normal.\n\nPHQ-9 2.\n\nA/P:\n1) Schizophrenia on clozapine: CBC/ANC and CK today as this cycle's monitoring draw; standing order renewed for every 2 weeks. Metabolic check: CMP, lipids, A1c today.\n2) Weight gain on clozapine: modest. Talked about portions and keeping up the gym; recheck at next visit.\n3) GSD IV: stable.\n4) Health maintenance: flu shot in the fall; covid vaccine offered, he will think about it. Td due 2031.\nReturn in 6 months, or sooner for anything."
